- `phishing_detector.py`

## Critical: No ulimit -v for Chromium

NEVER set `ulimit -v` (virtual memory limit) in any environment running Playwright/Chromium. Chromium's PartitionAlloc reserves 8-16 GB of virtual address space (not physical RAM). A virtual memory cap causes `partition_address_space.cc` to abort on startup. Use Docker `mem_limit` or systemd `MemoryMax` for actual memory enforcement instead.

## Subprocess Python Path

When spawning Python subprocesses (e.g., for detonation), always use `sys.executable` instead of `"python3"` to ensure the correct virtualenv interpreter is used.

